---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base wide title="About Us">
	<h1>About Us</h1>
	<div class="prose-text">
		<h2>Who We Are</h2>
		<p>
			Harmonic Bridges is a student-led organization dedicated to empowering young people to
			develop leadership skills, foster innovation, and make a meaningful impact through community
			service across King County, including Seattle, the Eastside, and North and South King County.
		</p>
		<p>
			Our three founders represent three different high schools across the county, providing a
			strong foundation for bringing together students from diverse backgrounds who share a
			commitment to service and community engagement. As passionate musicians and accomplished
			pianists, our founders aim to create music-centered outreach and educational opportunities
			that bridge generations, strengthen communities, and inspire lasting positive change.
		</p>
		<p>
			Our primary initiative is to organize concerts at senior centers throughout King County,
			bringing joy, comfort, and connection to seniors through music. We also plan to offer
			interactive music activities for seniors to encourage their lifelong learning, cognitive
			engagement, and social connection. Additionally, we aspire to partner with elementary
			schools and King County libraries to provide music enrichment opportunities for children who
			have limited access to music education. By expanding access to musical learning, we aim to
			promote educational equity, nurture young talents, and foster inclusion.
		</p>
		<p>
			Through these initiatives, we hope to make music a bridge between generations and a source
			of inspiration, connection, and opportunity for people of all ages. We welcome young leaders
			who share our passion for music, service, and community building to join us in bringing
			these initiatives to life and creating a more connected, inclusive, and vibrant King County.
		</p>

		<h2>Our Mission</h2>
		<p>Our mission is to build bridges between generations and communities through live music.</p>
		<p>We strive to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Connect through music</strong> by bringing live performances to senior living
				communities and local audiences.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Share music with purpose</strong> by using our musical abilities to create
				meaningful experiences for others.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Grow through collaboration</strong> by bringing student musicians together around a
				shared commitment to community service.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Make a lasting difference</strong> by developing a sustainable initiative that can
				reach more people and create more opportunities for connection.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Our Founding Team</h2>
		<p>
			Harmonic Bridges was built through the shared efforts of three student musicians, each
			contributing to a common vision.
		</p>
		<ul class="founders">
			<li>Emily Qi</li>
			<li>David Zhang</li>
			<li>William Feng</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="pending">Profiles to be added.</p>

		<h2>Looking Ahead</h2>
		<p>
			Harmonic Bridges is built on a simple idea: meaningful change can begin with a small act of
			sharing.
		</p>
		<p>
			What began with solo piano performances has grown into a shared effort to bring student
			musicians and community members together. As we continue this journey, we hope to expand our
			reach, welcome more opportunities for collaboration, and create more moments in which music
			helps people feel connected, valued, and inspired.
		</p>
		<p class="tagline">
			One shared passion. Three founding musicians. A growing community connected through music.
		</p>
	</div>

	<section class="band">
		<h2>Get in touch</h2>
		<p>
			Interested in hosting us, volunteering, or partnering? Use the links below — we read every
			message.
		</p>
		<div class="cta-row">
			<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/request-performance">Request a Performance</a>
			<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/get-involved">Get Involved</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>

<style>
	.prose-text {
		font-size: 1.1em;
		max-width: 65ch;
		margin-bottom: 2em;
	}
	.prose-text h2 {
		margin-top: 1.6em;
	}
	.prose-text li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
	.founders li {
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.pending {
		font-style: italic;
		opacity: 0.7;
	}
	.tagline {
		font-style: italic;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--accent-dark);
		margin-top: 1.5em;
	}
	.band {
		text-align: center;
		background: var(--brand-grad);
		border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
		padding: 3em 1.5em;
		margin-top: 3.5em;
		color: var(--cream);
		border-top: 4px solid var(--gold);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
	}
	.band :global(h2) {
		color: var(--cream);
	}
	.band p {
		max-width: 50ch;
		margin: 0.5em auto 1.5em;
		color: rgba(252, 245, 227, 0.9);
	}
	.band .btn-primary {
		background: var(--gold);
		color: var(--accent-dark);
		box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
	}
	.band .btn-primary:hover {
		color: var(--accent-dark);
	}
	.band .btn-secondary {
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
		color: var(--cream);
		border-color: rgba(252, 245, 227, 0.5);
	}
	.band .btn-secondary:hover {
		color: var(--gold);
		border-color: var(--gold);
	}
	.cta-row {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1em;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}
</style>
